blocks.text:
{"content":"# Thread 1 — task-ledger record bypasses the redaction pipeline

Fixed in `lib/src/cli/trajectory_commands.dart` (`_onTaskLedger`): when the host carries a `config.redactionPipeline`, every free-text field of every ledger item (`requirement`, `command`, `expected`, `actual`) is passed through `pipeline.redact` before `appendCustomEntry`, mirroring the sibling `_persistToolLivenessRecord` (gh-1054 convention). With no pipeline the record persists verbatim (byte-identical legacy).

```dart
final data = pipeline == null
    ? event.ledger.toJson()
    : {
        'items': [
          for (final item in event.ledger.items)
            {
              ...item.toJson(),
              'requirement': pipeline.redact(item.requirement),
              'command': pipeline.redact(item.command),
              'expected': pipeline.redact(item.expected),
              'actual': pipeline.redact(item.actual),
            },
        ],
      };
```

Regression test: `test/cli/finalize_gate_ledger_persist_test.dart` — an unattended headless run whose final answer's ledger embeds a registered secret; asserts the persisted `task_ledger` record carries no raw secret, carries `[REDACTED:` markers, keeps the structured `status` intact, and that a pipeline-less host still persists verbatim.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_01.md"}

{"content":"# Thread 4 — AGENTS.md names a symbol that does not exist

Fixed in `AGENTS.md`: the phantom `Agent.persistTaskLedger` is gone. The paragraph now names the real seams: `agent_event_handler.dart` → `_onTaskLedger` in `trajectory_commands.dart` (where the `appendCustomEntry` lives, redacted through the host pipeline), wired through `handleAgentEvent`'s nullable `onTaskLedger` callback — unset keeps interactive sessions ledger-less.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_04.md"}

{"content":"# Thread 7 — missing trailing newline in the task_ledger fixture

